    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Arunachal Pradesh transitioned from a Union Territory to a full-fledged State on 20th February 1987 under the 55th Constitutional Amendment Act.",
        "NEFA (North-East Frontier Agency) was renamed Arunachal Pradesh on 20th January 1972.",
        "Simla Accord (1914) established the McMahon Line as the boundary between Tibet and British India in this region."
      ],
      "id": "qa6tld2"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "In 1912–13, the British administration constituted the North-East Frontier Tracts (NEFT).",
        "In 1954, the administrative division was constitutionally designated as the North-East Frontier Agency (NEFA).",
        "On 20th January 1972, NEFA was renamed Arunachal Pradesh and granted Union Territory status.",
        "Arunachal Pradesh attained full statehood on 20th February 1987, becoming the 24th state of the Indian Union."
      ],
